    "lcm_examples_more": {
      "id": "lcm_examples_more",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "The objective section also gives several direct L.C.M. fraction patterns.\n\nOne is:\n\n2/3, 3/5, 4/7 and 9/13\n\nNumerator L.C.M.: L.C.M.(2,3,4,9) = 36\nDenominator H.C.F.: H.C.F.(3,5,7,13) = 1\n\nTherefore:\n\nL.C.M. = 36/1 = 36\n\nWhen the denominator H.C.F. is 1, the final result is simply the numerator L.C.M.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "lcm_more_check"
        }
