      "id": "least_fraction_intro",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Now we reach a useful application from the objective solutions. The question asks for a fraction that is divisible by each of several given fractions.\n\nThe chapter's solution uses the L.C.M. formula for fractions.\n\nExample:\n\nFind the required fraction for 6/7, 5/14 and 10/21.\n\nThe answer is formed as:\n\nL.C.M. of numerators / H.C.F. of denominators\n\nSo we use:\n\nL.C.M.(6,5,10) and H.C.F.(7,14,21).",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
