    "final_recap": {
      "id": "final_recap",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "You now have the complete fraction rules from this chapter.\n\nH.C.F. of fractions = H.C.F. of numerators / L.C.M. of denominators\n\nL.C.M. of fractions = L.C.M. of numerators / H.C.F. of denominators\n\nFor any number of fractions:\nseparate all numerators from all denominators, perform the required H.C.F./L.C.M. operation on each group, and then form the resulting fraction.\n\nRemember the direction:\n\nH.C.F. → H.C.F. on top, L.C.M. below.\nL.C.M. → L.C.M. on top, H.C.F. below.\n\nThe chapter also applies the second rule to the required fraction divisible by 6/7, 5/14 and 10/21, giving 30/7.\n\nThat is the whole pattern. Once the formula is identified correctly, the rest is just two ordinary H.C.F./L.C.M. calculations.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
